+The augmented refinement reduces the population mean $\mathcal M_S$ by 80.2\% relative to the original DGF checkpoint and by 37.8\% relative to the first refinement. The paired mean differences are $-0.02178$ and $-0.003257$, with 95\% percentile bootstrap intervals $[-0.02697,-0.01696]$ and $[-0.00535,-0.00134]$, respectively. These intervals use a fixed bootstrap seed (20261009) and 5000 paired resamples of the test examples and quantify sampling variation for the fixed fitted checkpoints; they are not estimates of training-seed variability. Figure~\ref{fig:mismatch} shows the complete empirical distributions. The mean, median, and upper percentiles characterize different aspects of the error tail and should not be interchanged.
